course: dictionary
lesson: 10919
title: Volcano: active, dormant or extinct
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A volcano is a mountain or an opening in the Earth's surface where hot melted rock, ash and gases come out from deep inside. Words around it give clues. «Lava from a volcano is rock so hot that it has melted into a liquid.» So lava is the melted rock that flows out, and when it cools it freezes back into solid rock.
explain: Volcanoes are often described by how they behave. An active volcano can still erupt. A dormant volcano is sleeping and might erupt again. An extinct volcano is not expected to erupt again. Look at the word before volcano to find the clue.
explain: «In AD 79 the volcano Vesuvius buried the town of Pompeii in ash.» Ash is the fine powder that flew out in the eruption. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: A volcano is a mountain or opening in the Earth's surface where hot melted rock, ash and gases come out.
fact: Lava is hot melted rock that comes out of a volcano; while it is still underground, it is called magma.
fact: An active volcano can erupt; a dormant volcano is sleeping and might erupt again; an extinct volcano is not expected to erupt again.
fact: Volcanoes often form where tectonic plates meet, or over hot spots deep in the Earth.
fact: «Mount Everest» is the highest mountain above sea level, but «Mauna Kea», a volcano in Hawaii, is taller when measured from its base on the sea floor.
exercise: «Lava from a volcano is rock so hot that it has melted into a liquid.» What is lava? | *Hot melted rock that flows out of a volcano | A gas that smells of eggs | A kind of cloud | Cold ash that falls from the sky
exercise: What does dormant mean for a volcano? | *It is sleeping and might erupt again | It is full of foam | It is making lava right now | It can never erupt again, like a volcano that is gone
exercise: «In AD 79 the volcano Vesuvius buried the town of Pompeii in ash.» Find and copy one word that names what buried Pompeii. | Vesuvius | AD | town | *ash
test: «Washing-up liquid in a model volcano traps the carbon dioxide in bubbles and makes foam.» In a model volcano, what does the washing-up liquid make? | Solid rock | Ash clouds | *Foam | Lava that cools into stone
test: «Mauna Kea, a volcano in Hawaii, is taller measured from its base on the sea floor.» Which volcano is taller when measured from its base? | *Mauna Kea | Vesuvius | Mount Everest | Mount Ruapehu
exam: Jayden reads «The volcano was dormant for centuries, then it erupted.» What does dormant mean here? | Full of foam | *Sleeping for a long time, though it can still wake up and erupt | Dead for ever, so it can never erupt again | Making lava right now
